.\" Man page for himalaya-mcp CLI
.\" Generated: July 2026
.TH HIMALAYA-MCP 1 "July 2026" "himalaya-mcp 1.9.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
himalaya\-mcp \- Privacy-first email MCP server and Claude Code plugin (CLI)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B himalaya-mcp
[\fIcommand\fR] [\fIflags\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B himalaya-mcp
is the unified command-line interface for the himalaya-mcp package
— a privacy-first email MCP server that wraps the
.B himalaya
CLI.
.PP
The CLI manages Claude Desktop integration, installs/removes the
.B .mcpb
Desktop extension, and provides a diagnostic
.B doctor
command that probes the full installation stack.
.PP
Run with no arguments (or
.BR setup )
to add the himalaya MCP server to Claude Desktop's
configuration.
.SH COMMANDS
.SS Setup (Claude Desktop)
.TP
.B setup
Add the himalaya MCP server entry to Claude Desktop's config file.
This is the default when no command is given.
.TP
.B check\fR, \fBsetup --check
Verify the Claude Desktop config exists and the himalaya entry
is present with a valid
.B dist/index.js
path.
.TP
.B remove\fR, \fBsetup --remove
Remove the himalaya MCP server entry from Claude Desktop config.
Idempotent: succeeds with a notice if nothing to remove.
.SS Desktop Extension (.mcpb)
.TP
.B install-ext
[\fIfile\fR]
Install a
.B .mcpb
Desktop extension into Claude Desktop.
Auto-discovers
.B himalaya-mcp-v*.mcpb
in the project root if
.I file
is omitted. Re-registers the extension in
.B extensions-installations.json
and creates default settings.
.TP
.B remove-ext
Remove the himalaya-mcp Desktop extension directory, settings file,
and registry entry. Idempotent.
.SS Network (Streamable HTTP)
.TP
.B serve
Listen for remote MCP clients on Streamable HTTP. Requires a bearer
token. Local Claude and Codex installs keep using stdio and are unchanged.
.RS
.TP
.B --host \fIaddr\fR
Bind address. Default
.BR 127.0.0.1 ,
or
.BR MCP_HOST .
Use
.B 0.0.0.0
to accept connections from other machines.
.TP
.B --port \fIn\fR
TCP port. Default 8080, or
.BR MCP_PORT .
.TP
.B --path \fIpath\fR
MCP endpoint path. Default
.BR /mcp .
.TP
.B --token-file \fIfile\fR
Read the bearer token from a file instead of the environment.
.TP
.B --sse
Send SSE responses. The default is one JSON body per POST, which remote
tool proxies accept reliably.
.RE
.PP
Every request to the MCP path must send
.BR "Authorization: Bearer <token>" .
.B GET /health
is unauthenticated and returns process liveness only.
Composio custom MCP uses API-key auth with header
.BR "Authorization: Bearer {{generic_api_key}}"
and
.B app_url
set to the public HTTPS URL of this path. Terminate TLS with a reverse
proxy or tunnel; Composio does not accept a plain HTTP URL.
.SS Diagnostics
.TP
.B doctor
Run the full diagnostic suite: prerequisites, MCP server, email
connectivity, Desktop extension, Claude Code plugin, plugin cache,
environment, and per-account reachability.
.RS
.TP
.B --account \fIname\fR
Run checks for a specific account only.
.TP
.B --fix
Auto-fix common issues (writes default settings, sets
.B himalaa_binary
path, prunes stale plugin cache).
.TP
.B --json
Emit machine-readable JSON of all check results.
.RE
.SS Meta
.TP
.B --help\fR, \fB-h\fR, \fBhelp
Print versioned usage message on stdout and exit 0.
.TP
.B --version\fR, \fB-v\fR, \fBversion
Print the semantic version on stdout and exit 0.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/Library/Application Support/Claude/claude_desktop_config.json
(macOS) Claude Desktop MCP server config; modified by
.BR setup
and
.BR remove .
.TP
.I ~/Library/Application Support/Claude/Claude Extensions/himalaya-mcp/
(macOS) Claude Desktop extension directory; created by
.BR install-ext
and removed by
.BR remove-ext .
.TP
.I ~/.claude/plugins/himalaya-mcp/
Claude Code plugin directory (real copy after
.BR brew upgrade ;
previously a symlink).
.TP
.I ~/.claude/local-marketplace/.claude-plugin/marketplace.json
Local marketplace manifest populated by
.BR himalaya-mcp-install .
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B HIMALAYA_BINARY
Path to the
.B himalaya
binary (default: looks up
.B himalaya
on
.BR PATH ).
.TP
.B HIMALAYA_ACCOUNT
Default email account name (default: himalaya system default).
.TP
.B HIMALAYA_FOLDER
Default folder (default:
.BR INBOX ).
.TP
.B HIMALAYA_TIMEOUT
Command timeout in ms (default: 120000, i.e. 2 min; 0 = unlimited).
.TP
.B MCP_BEARER_TOKEN
Shared secret for
.BR serve .
At least 16 characters. Removed from the environment before himalaya is
spawned. Prefer
.B MCP_BEARER_TOKEN_FILE
so the secret is not in the process environment at all.
.TP
.B MCP_BEARER_TOKEN_FILE
File containing the bearer token. Trailing whitespace is stripped.
.TP
.B MCP_HOST
Bind address for
.BR serve .
Default
.BR 127.0.0.1 .
.TP
.B MCP_PORT
Port for
.BR serve .
Default 8080.
.TP
.B MCP_PATH
MCP endpoint path. Default
.BR /mcp .
.TP
.B MCP_TRANSPORT
Set to
.B http
to make
.B node dist/index.js
listen on HTTP instead of stdio. Do not set this in the Claude plugin
environment.
.TP
.B MCP_HTTP_JSON
Set to
.B false
for SSE POST responses. Default is JSON.
.SH EXAMPLES
First-time install:
.RS
.nf
himalaya-mcp setup
.fi
.RE
.PP
Verify everything is working:
.RS
.nf
himalaya-mcp doctor
himalaya-mcp doctor \-\-account work
himalaya-mcp doctor \-\-fix
himalaya-mcp doctor \-\-json | jq .
.fi
.RE
.PP
Install as Claude Desktop Extension:
.RS
.nf
npm run build:mcpb
himalaya-mcp install-ext
.fi
.RE
.PP
Uninstall:
.RS
.nf
himalaya-mcp remove-ext
himalaya-mcp remove
.fi
.RE
.PP
Serve MCP for Composio (then publish the URL over HTTPS):
.RS
.nf
export MCP_BEARER_TOKEN="$(openssl rand -hex 32)"
himalaya-mcp serve --host 127.0.0.1 --port 8080
.fi
.RE
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Generic failure (check command not found, IMAP auth failed, missing
prerequisite, etc.). See stderr or
.B doctor
output for details.
